/target
/data/corpus/dataset.csv
/data/click/
/data/shot/
/data/figures/
.suite-corpus.pid
.suite-corpus.log
.suite.pid
.suite.log
# Conjunto C7: scripts/app replaces scripts/dash + scripts/studio (one
# binary now, see the design notes ┬º10 C7).
.app.pid
.app.log
.app.port
# Saved layer stacks. A property of the operator's act rather than of the repo,
# the same way outputs.json is a property of the room.
data/collections.json

# The one-way conversion of collections.json into graphs, written once at
# startup (the design notes Conjunto B6). Same reason as collections.json
# above: it's a projection of the operator's own data, not the repo's.
data/graphs/

# Modo edit's shows: which generator and which effects are alive over which
# span of ticks, plus whatever `POST /timeline/export` wrote beside them.
# A show is the operator's work, like a collection ÔÇö the repo has no business
# carrying one, and a pre-produced piece for a venue is not something to
# commit by accident.
data/timelines/

# The song library and its 8 Hz digests. Someone else's copyright, hundreds of
# megabytes, and a checkout does not need them ÔÇö `click-100` is tracked because
# the harnesses need one song to open, and the rest is the operator's own crate.
# This is also why a trained router `model.json` must be committed when there is
# one: it cannot be rebuilt from a checkout, because the audio it was fit to is
# not in it. See docs/ROUTER.md.
/data/audio/*
!/data/audio/click-100.toml
!/data/audio/click-100.wav

# A transmission's frame ladder. Hundreds of megabytes of proxy JPEGs derived
# from footage that is not in the repo either, and rebuildable in one command
# from the folder it came from (`metal-reel index`). The `index.json` beside it
# stays tracked ÔÇö it is a few hundred kilobytes and it is what makes a library
# usable without re-extracting.
#
# `curator.json` and `colourist-*.json` must be committed when they exist, for
# exactly the reason `docs/ROUTER.md` gives about `model.json`: they are fitted
# against picks *and* the songs' 8 Hz matrices, and a fresh checkout has neither,
# so the file is the only copy of a night of authoring.
/data/reels/*/frames/

# Test scratch. `author::models::agent_tools` tests write `data/reels/<name>/`
# and `data/timelines/` relative to the cwd `cargo test` gives them, which is
# the crate dir ÔÇö two of those files were committed by accident in Ola 1 and
# "restored" once by S.U4b as if they were fixtures. They are not: the tests
# build them. Same for whatever the JS harnesses leave when run from here.
crates/metal-dash/data/

# Claude Code's own worktrees for parallel subagents ÔÇö local state, never
# part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/

# Graphify's derived side ÔÇö a local index, rebuilt on demand, never tracked.
/graphify-out/

# Chat transcripts Claude Code leaves behind.
/data/chats/

# ML model binaries. Not committed (D9): each is fetched on demand into its
# registry folder and hash-checked against the sibling model.toml. The folder
# and its model.toml stay tracked; only the .onnx blob is ignored.
data/models/*/model.onnx
!data/models/basic-pitch/model.onnx

__pycache__/

# The operator's AI provider config (holds the raw API key) and per-tool
# policy ÔÇö local, the same "operator's own data" rule as collections.json.
# A fresh checkout has no provider until the settings IA page writes one.
/data/ai.json
/data/ai_tools.json
/secrets/

# Packed into the APK by scripts/build-apk.sh (a copy of part of data/).
/android/app/src/main/assets/
web/wasm/pkg/

